[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `double` reaches stdout through `%.2f`, which collapses whole classes of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m distinct values (all NaNs, everything below `0.005`) onto the same text.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **End-to-end** — both binaries run as subprocesses with identical `argv`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    stdout, stderr and exit status compared byte for byte. 34,696 cases.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **`strtod` in isolation** — a C probe and a Rust probe print
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `(value bits, endptr offset, errno == ERANGE)` for the same byte string.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    487,820 inputs (476,740 non-empty), covering a random lexical grammar fuzz,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    well-formed decimals across the full exponent range, the exact decimal
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    expansions of the low subnormals and of the values bracketing `DBL_MIN` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `DBL_MAX`, exact midpoints between consecutive subnormals, hex forms across
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    every binade, all `inf`/`nan` spellings, and raw random bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **`pow` + `%.2f` in isolation** — same idea, printing
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `(result bits, errno, %.2f of result, base and exponent)`. 718,699 operand
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    pairs.
