[38;5;252m[1m## Findings[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe delivered [38;5;10mmain.rs[0m was not the translation.[22m It declared [38;5;10mstrtod[0m, [38;5;10mpow[0m and [38;5;10m__errno_location[0m as [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m and called libc directly, so [38;5;10msrc/strtod.rs[0m, [38;5;10msrc/cpow.rs[0m and [38;5;10msrc/cfmt.rs[0m — documented as faithful reimplementations — were dead code that nothing compiled or checked. I rebuilt the original in a scratch crate and confirmed it produced no output mismatch (0 of 34,696 cases), so this was a structural defect, not a behavioural one. [38;5;10mmain.rs[0m now routes through the modules. [38;5;10mnm -D[0m confirms the binary no longer imports [38;5;10mstrtod[0m; the one remaining libm import is [38;5;10mpow@GLIBC_2.29[0m, the same symbol the C binary uses and how [38;5;10mf64::powf[0m is implemented on this target.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mOne real bit-level mismatch, in that dead code:[22m [38;5;10mstrtod[0m discarded the [38;5;10mnan(<payload>)[0m bitmask, returning a bare quiet NaN. 36 of 476,740 isolated inputs diverged. glibc runs the parenthesised sequence through [38;5;10mstrtoull(seq, &end, 0)[0m and, only if that consumes all of it, ORs the low 51 bits into the mantissa — which is why [38;5;10mnan(010)[0m is 8 (octal), [38;5;10mnan(08)[0m is 0 (not fully consumed), and [38;5;10mnan(0x8000000000000)[0m is 0 (bit 51 is the quiet bit). Fixed in [38;5;10msrc/strtod.rs[0m. This was invisible in stdout, since [38;5;10m%.2f[0m renders every NaN as [38;5;10mnan[0m/[38;5;10m-nan[0m from the sign bit alone — but the adjacent case matters: a payload that overflows [38;5;10mstrtoull[0m would have surfaced as [38;5;10mRange error while converting base[0m if glibc leaked that [38;5;10mERANGE[0m. I checked; it does not.[0m[0m
